    "For U3: Profile JobLaunchingTasklet execution to identify bottlenecks; refactor by introducing asynchronous processing, batching, or caching where appropriate, while maintaining backward compatibility.",
    "For U4: Adopt parameterized JUnit 5 tests to cover DSL and XML generation variants; use Spring's test context framework for integration tests; enforce coverage thresholds via JaCoCo.",
    "For U5: Integrate Spring Expression Language (SpEL) parser into the stream definition DSL; evaluate expressions against the message payload at runtime; ensure security by restricting SpEL functions.",
    "For U6: Author job orchestration documentation in AsciiDoc format, following the project's existing documentation structure; include examples for batch workflow construction.",
    "For U7: Extend the YARN SPI status enum with an UNDEPLOYED value; modify the YARN state reconciliation logic to return this status when an application is not deployed.",
    "For U8: Split the admin artifact into multiple Maven modules, one per supported Hadoop distribution (e.g., HDP, CDH, Apache); use Maven profiles to control dependency inclusion; update dependent projects to reference the new modules."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The project is a Spring Integration / Spring Cloud Data Flow related codebase using Java 17+, Maven or Gradle, and JUnit 5.",
